{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# MMCA-Detect \u2014 Synthetic Feasibility Study (Appendix A)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Companion notebook to:** *MMCA-Detect: A Multi-Modal Cross-Attention Architecture for Adversarial Attack Detection in Autonomous Vehicle Perception \u2014 Architecture, Theory, and a Synthetic-Data Feasibility Study* (Rohit Joshi).\n",
    "\n",
    "> \u26a0\ufe0f **Read this before running.** This notebook reproduces **Appendix A** of the paper exactly: a small, CPU-only, synthetic-data feasibility check of the training/evaluation code paths for five model configurations. It does **not** train or evaluate on real camera, LiDAR, or radar data, and it does **not** reproduce any real adversarial attack (FGSM/PGD/C&W/physical-patch/LiDAR-spoofing). \"Adversarial\" samples here are synthetic tensors nudged by a fixed random direction \u2014 a toy stand-in used only to check that the code and models are learnable end-to-end. Every number this notebook produces should be read exactly as Section VI of the paper reads them: **feasibility-check output, not a measurement of real-world adversarial-detection performance.**\n",
    "\n",
    "Running this notebook top-to-bottom reproduces Tables II\u2013III and Figures 4\u20135 of the paper (numbers will vary slightly run-to-run unless you keep the same seeds, which this notebook does by default).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Runtime:** CPU is sufficient and is what the paper's latency numbers are based on \u2014 in Colab, use `Runtime > Change runtime type > CPU` (a GPU runtime will still work but latency figures would then not match the paper, which reports CPU wall-clock time). Total run time is a few minutes.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 0. Setup\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Colab ships with torch, numpy, scikit-learn, pandas, and matplotlib pre-installed.\n",
    "# This cell is a safety net in case any are missing or out of date \u2014 safe to run either way.\n",
    "!pip install -q torch numpy scikit-learn pandas matplotlib\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import time\n",
    "import json\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import torch\n",
    "import torch.nn as nn\n",
    "from torch.utils.data import DataLoader, TensorDataset\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import confusion_matrix, roc_auc_score\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "torch.set_num_threads(4)\n",
    "DEVICE = \"cpu\"  # paper's latency figures are CPU wall-clock; keep this as \"cpu\" to match Section VI\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"PyTorch {torch.__version__}, running on {DEVICE}\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Synthetic Data Generation\n",
    "\n",
    "Matches paper Section V-B / Appendix A exactly: for each seeded run, `num_samples` clean tensors are drawn i.i.d. standard normal for each modality \u2014 camera `3\u00d764\u00d764`, LiDAR `256\u00d73`, radar `64\u00d74`. A **fixed random unit-norm direction per modality per run** is scaled to L2 norm 3.0 and added to each clean sample, plus small residual Gaussian noise (\u03c3 = 0.05), to build the \"adversarial\" counterpart. This gives a *structured, bounded, learnable* perturbation \u2014 deliberately chosen over pure unstructured per-sample noise, which the paper separately notes carries no learnable class signal at all under this data-generating process (Section VII-B).\n",
    "\n",
    "Labels are balanced (50% clean / 50% adversarial). Data is split 70/15/15 into train/validation/test.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def make_dataset(num_samples=500, seed=0):\n",
    "    g = torch.Generator().manual_seed(seed)\n",
    "    camera_clean = torch.randn(num_samples, 3, 64, 64, generator=g)\n",
    "    lidar_clean = torch.randn(num_samples, 256, 3, generator=g)\n",
    "    radar_clean = torch.randn(num_samples, 64, 4, generator=g)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Structured synthetic perturbation: a fixed random direction per run,\n",
    "    # scaled to a bounded epsilon and applied consistently to all\n",
    "    # \"adversarial\" samples (a toy analogue of a bounded, direction-\n",
    "    # consistent attack such as FGSM, in contrast to unstructured\n",
    "    # independent noise which carries no learnable class signal).\n",
    "    dir_c = torch.randn(3, 64, 64, generator=g); dir_c = dir_c / dir_c.norm()\n",
    "    dir_l = torch.randn(256, 3, generator=g); dir_l = dir_l / dir_l.norm()\n",
    "    dir_r = torch.randn(64, 4, generator=g); dir_r = dir_r / dir_r.norm()\n",
    "\n",
    "    eps_c, eps_l, eps_r = 3.0, 3.0, 3.0  # bounded perturbation magnitude (L2, toy units)\n",
    "    camera_adv = camera_clean + eps_c * dir_c + torch.randn(num_samples, 3, 64, 64, generator=g) * 0.05\n",
    "    lidar_adv = lidar_clean + eps_l * dir_l + torch.randn(num_samples, 256, 3, generator=g) * 0.05\n",
    "    radar_adv = radar_clean + eps_r * dir_r + torch.randn(num_samples, 64, 4, generator=g) * 0.05\n",
    "\n",
    "    camera = torch.cat([camera_clean, camera_adv], dim=0)\n",
    "    lidar = torch.cat([lidar_clean, lidar_adv], dim=0)\n",
    "    radar = torch.cat([radar_clean, radar_adv], dim=0)\n",
    "    labels = torch.cat([torch.zeros(num_samples), torch.ones(num_samples)])\n",
    "\n",
    "    total = len(labels)\n",
    "    perm = torch.randperm(total, generator=g)\n",
    "    train_n = int(0.7 * total)\n",
    "    val_n = int(0.15 * total)\n",
    "    idx_tr, idx_va, idx_te = perm[:train_n], perm[train_n:train_n + val_n], perm[train_n + val_n:]\n",
    "\n",
    "    def subset(idx):\n",
    "        return TensorDataset(camera[idx], lidar[idx], radar[idx], labels[idx])\n",
    "\n",
    "    return subset(idx_tr), subset(idx_va), subset(idx_te)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Quick sanity check\n",
    "_tr, _va, _te = make_dataset(num_samples=500, seed=100)\n",
    "print(f\"train={len(_tr)}  val={len(_va)}  test={len(_te)}  (total should be 1000 = 2\\u00d7500)\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Model Configurations\n",
    "\n",
    "Five configurations, matching paper Section V-C / Appendix A:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Configuration | Modalities used | Fusion | Params |\n",
    "|---|---|---|---|\n",
    "| Camera-only | Camera | \u2014 (single modality) | 16,225 |\n",
    "| Simple-concatenation | Cam + LiDAR + Radar | Feature concatenation, no attention | 80,385 |\n",
    "| Cross-attention (full) | Cam + LiDAR + Radar | `nn.MultiheadAttention`, 4 heads, d=64 | 97,025 |\n",
    "| Cross-attention (w/o LiDAR) | Cam + Radar | Same cross-attention, 2 modalities | 43,713 |\n",
    "| Cross-attention (w/o radar) | Cam + LiDAR | Same cross-attention, 2 modalities | 76,481 |\n",
    "\n",
    "This is a deliberately compact, CPU-sized version of the target production architecture in paper Section IV-B (which specifies ResNet-50 / PointNet++ / a larger MLP, 31.2M parameters total) \u2014 sized down here only to keep the feasibility check fast and inexpensive, per Section V-D.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class CamOnly(nn.Module):\n",
    "    def __init__(self):\n",
    "        super().__init__()\n",
    "        self.enc = nn.Sequential(\n",
    "            nn.Conv2d(3, 16, 5, stride=2, padding=2), nn.ReLU(),\n",
    "            nn.Conv2d(16, 32, 5, stride=2, padding=2), nn.ReLU(),\n",
    "            nn.AdaptiveAvgPool2d(1), nn.Flatten(),\n",
    "            nn.Linear(32, 64), nn.ReLU(), nn.Linear(64, 1),\n",
    "        )\n",
    "\n",
    "    def forward(self, cam, lidar, radar):\n",
    "        return self.enc(cam)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "class SimpleConcat(nn.Module):\n",
    "    def __init__(self):\n",
    "        super().__init__()\n",
    "        self.cam = nn.Sequential(\n",
    "            nn.Conv2d(3, 16, 5, stride=2, padding=2), nn.ReLU(),\n",
    "            nn.AdaptiveAvgPool2d(1), nn.Flatten(), nn.Linear(16, 64))\n",
    "        self.lid = nn.Linear(256 * 3, 64)\n",
    "        self.rad = nn.Linear(64 * 4, 64)\n",
    "        self.head = nn.Sequential(nn.Linear(192, 64), nn.ReLU(), nn.Linear(64, 1))\n",
    "\n",
    "    def forward(self, cam, lidar, radar):\n",
    "        f = torch.cat([self.cam(cam), self.lid(lidar.flatten(1)), self.rad(radar.flatten(1))], dim=1)\n",
    "        return self.head(f)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "class CrossAttnFusion(nn.Module):\n",
    "    def __init__(self, d=64):\n",
    "        super().__init__()\n",
    "        self.cam = nn.Sequential(\n",
    "            nn.Conv2d(3, 16, 5, stride=2, padding=2), nn.ReLU(),\n",
    "            nn.AdaptiveAvgPool2d(1), nn.Flatten(), nn.Linear(16, d))\n",
    "        self.lid = nn.Linear(256 * 3, d)\n",
    "        self.rad = nn.Linear(64 * 4, d)\n",
    "        self.attn = nn.MultiheadAttention(d, num_heads=4, batch_first=True)\n",
    "        self.head = nn.Sequential(nn.Linear(d * 3, 64), nn.ReLU(), nn.Dropout(0.2), nn.Linear(64, 1))\n",
    "\n",
    "    def forward(self, cam, lidar, radar):\n",
    "        f_c, f_l, f_r = self.cam(cam), self.lid(lidar.flatten(1)), self.rad(radar.flatten(1))\n",
    "        feats = torch.stack([f_c, f_l, f_r], dim=1)\n",
    "        attended, _ = self.attn(feats, feats, feats)\n",
    "        return self.head(attended.flatten(1))\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "class CrossAttnNoLidar(nn.Module):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Ablation: camera + radar only (LiDAR branch removed).\"\"\"\n",
    "    def __init__(self, d=64):\n",
    "        super().__init__()\n",
    "        self.cam = nn.Sequential(\n",
    "            nn.Conv2d(3, 16, 5, stride=2, padding=2), nn.ReLU(),\n",
    "            nn.AdaptiveAvgPool2d(1), nn.Flatten(), nn.Linear(16, d))\n",
    "        self.rad = nn.Linear(64 * 4, d)\n",
    "        self.attn = nn.MultiheadAttention(d, num_heads=4, batch_first=True)\n",
    "        self.head = nn.Sequential(nn.Linear(d * 2, 64), nn.ReLU(), nn.Dropout(0.2), nn.Linear(64, 1))\n",
    "\n",
    "    def forward(self, cam, lidar, radar):\n",
    "        f_c, f_r = self.cam(cam), self.rad(radar.flatten(1))\n",
    "        feats = torch.stack([f_c, f_r], dim=1)\n",
    "        attended, _ = self.attn(feats, feats, feats)\n",
    "        return self.head(attended.flatten(1))\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "class CrossAttnNoRadar(nn.Module):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Ablation: camera + LiDAR only (radar branch removed).\"\"\"\n",
    "    def __init__(self, d=64):\n",
    "        super().__init__()\n",
    "        self.cam = nn.Sequential(\n",
    "            nn.Conv2d(3, 16, 5, stride=2, padding=2), nn.ReLU(),\n",
    "            nn.AdaptiveAvgPool2d(1), nn.Flatten(), nn.Linear(16, d))\n",
    "        self.lid = nn.Linear(256 * 3, d)\n",
    "        self.attn = nn.MultiheadAttention(d, num_heads=4, batch_first=True)\n",
    "        self.head = nn.Sequential(nn.Linear(d * 2, 64), nn.ReLU(), nn.Dropout(0.2), nn.Linear(64, 1))\n",
    "\n",
    "    def forward(self, cam, lidar, radar):\n",
    "        f_c, f_l = self.cam(cam), self.lid(lidar.flatten(1))\n",
    "        feats = torch.stack([f_c, f_l], dim=1)\n",
    "        attended, _ = self.attn(feats, feats, feats)\n",
    "        return self.head(attended.flatten(1))\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# Parameter counts, for cross-checking against the table above\n",
    "for _name, _ctor in [(\"Camera-only\", CamOnly), (\"Simple-concatenation\", SimpleConcat),\n",
    "                      (\"Cross-attention (full)\", CrossAttnFusion),\n",
    "                      (\"Cross-attention (w/o LiDAR)\", CrossAttnNoLidar),\n",
    "                      (\"Cross-attention (w/o radar)\", CrossAttnNoRadar)]:\n",
    "    _n = sum(p.numel() for p in _ctor().parameters())\n",
    "    print(f\"{_name:<32}{_n:>10,} parameters\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Training and Evaluation Protocol\n",
    "\n",
    "Matches paper Section V-D exactly: Adam (lr = 1e-3), batch size 32, 6 epochs, plain binary cross-entropy loss \u2014 **no** consistency-regularization term and **no** adversarial (PGD) training, since this feasibility check deliberately isolates whether the base architecture and fusion mechanism are learnable end-to-end, separate from the additional training techniques proposed for production use (paper Section IV-E).\n",
    "\n",
    "Evaluation on the held-out test split reports TPR, FPR, precision, F1, AUC-ROC (via scikit-learn), and per-sample latency (CPU wall-clock forward-pass time, batch-divided). Each configuration is run 3 times with different seeds (both data generation and model initialization); we report mean \u00b1 std with no run exclusion, cherry-picking, or post-hoc adjustment.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def train_and_eval(model_ctor, train_ds, val_ds, test_ds, epochs=6, seed=0):\n",
    "    torch.manual_seed(seed)\n",
    "    model = model_ctor().to(DEVICE)\n",
    "    opt = torch.optim.Adam(model.parameters(), lr=1e-3)\n",
    "    crit = nn.BCEWithLogitsLoss()\n",
    "    tl = DataLoader(train_ds, batch_size=32, shuffle=True)\n",
    "    for _ in range(epochs):\n",
    "        model.train()\n",
    "        for cam, lidar, radar, y in tl:\n",
    "            opt.zero_grad()\n",
    "            out = model(cam, lidar, radar).squeeze(-1)\n",
    "            loss = crit(out, y)\n",
    "            loss.backward()\n",
    "            opt.step()\n",
    "\n",
    "    model.eval()\n",
    "    te = DataLoader(test_ds, batch_size=32, shuffle=False)\n",
    "    preds, labels, scores, lat = [], [], [], []\n",
    "    with torch.no_grad():\n",
    "        for cam, lidar, radar, y in te:\n",
    "            t0 = time.perf_counter()\n",
    "            out = model(cam, lidar, radar).squeeze(-1)\n",
    "            t1 = time.perf_counter()\n",
    "            lat.append((t1 - t0) * 1000.0 / cam.shape[0])\n",
    "            p = torch.sigmoid(out)\n",
    "            preds.extend((p > 0.5).float().numpy())\n",
    "            labels.extend(y.numpy())\n",
    "            scores.extend(p.numpy())\n",
    "\n",
    "    preds, labels, scores = np.array(preds), np.array(labels), np.array(scores)\n",
    "    tn, fp, fn, tp = confusion_matrix(labels, preds).ravel()\n",
    "    tpr = tp / (tp + fn)\n",
    "    fpr = fp / (fp + tn)\n",
    "    precision = tp / (tp + fp) if (tp + fp) > 0 else 0.0\n",
    "    f1 = 2 * precision * tpr / (precision + tpr) if (precision + tpr) > 0 else 0.0\n",
    "    auc = roc_auc_score(labels, scores)\n",
    "    n_params = sum(p.numel() for p in model.parameters())\n",
    "    return dict(tpr=tpr, fpr=fpr, precision=precision, f1=f1, auc=auc,\n",
    "                latency_ms=float(np.mean(lat)), n_params=n_params)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def run_multi_seed(model_ctor, name, n_runs=3):\n",
    "    results = []\n",
    "    for run in range(n_runs):\n",
    "        train_ds, val_ds, test_ds = make_dataset(num_samples=500, seed=100 + run)\n",
    "        r = train_and_eval(model_ctor, train_ds, val_ds, test_ds, epochs=6, seed=run)\n",
    "        results.append(r)\n",
    "        print(f\"  [{name}] run {run+1}/{n_runs}: TPR={r['tpr']*100:.1f}% FPR={r['fpr']*100:.1f}% \"\n",
    "              f\"F1={r['f1']:.3f} AUC={r['auc']:.3f} lat={r['latency_ms']:.3f}ms\")\n",
    "    agg = {}\n",
    "    for k in [\"tpr\", \"fpr\", \"precision\", \"f1\", \"auc\", \"latency_ms\"]:\n",
    "        vals = [r[k] for r in results]\n",
    "        agg[k + \"_mean\"] = float(np.mean(vals))\n",
    "        agg[k + \"_std\"] = float(np.std(vals))\n",
    "    agg[\"n_params\"] = results[0][\"n_params\"]\n",
    "    return agg\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Run the Feasibility Study\n",
    "\n",
    "Runs all five configurations \u00d7 3 seeded runs each (15 short training runs total, CPU only). Takes a few minutes in a standard Colab CPU runtime.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"Running feasibility study (synthetic proxy data, CPU, 3 seeds per configuration)...\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "configs = {\n",
    "    \"Camera-only\": CamOnly,\n",
    "    \"Simple-concatenation\": SimpleConcat,\n",
    "    \"Cross-attention (full)\": CrossAttnFusion,\n",
    "    \"Cross-attention (w/o LiDAR)\": CrossAttnNoLidar,\n",
    "    \"Cross-attention (w/o radar)\": CrossAttnNoRadar,\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "all_results = {}\n",
    "for name, ctor in configs.items():\n",
    "    print(f\"Configuration: {name}\")\n",
    "    all_results[name] = run_multi_seed(ctor, name, n_runs=3)\n",
    "    print()\n",
    "\n",
    "with open(\"simulation_results.json\", \"w\") as f:\n",
    "    json.dump(all_results, f, indent=2)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Saved simulation_results.json\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Results Table (paper Table II)\n",
    "\n",
    "If you kept the default seeds, this should closely match Table II in the paper. Small differences are expected across PyTorch versions / hardware even with fixed seeds; that variation is itself consistent with the paper's point that these are low-confidence, small-n feasibility numbers, not tight measurements (Section VI-A).\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "rows = []\n",
    "for name, r in all_results.items():\n",
    "    rows.append({\n",
    "        \"Configuration\": name,\n",
    "        \"TPR%\": f\"{r['tpr_mean']*100:.1f}\\u00b1{r['tpr_std']*100:.1f}\",\n",
    "        \"FPR%\": f\"{r['fpr_mean']*100:.1f}\\u00b1{r['fpr_std']*100:.1f}\",\n",
    "        \"Precision\": f\"{r['precision_mean']:.3f}\",\n",
    "        \"F1\": f\"{r['f1_mean']:.3f}\",\n",
    "        \"AUC\": f\"{r['auc_mean']:.3f}\",\n",
    "        \"Latency (ms)\": f\"{r['latency_ms_mean']:.3f}\",\n",
    "        \"Params\": f\"{r['n_params']:,}\",\n",
    "    })\n",
    "df = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n",
    "df\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Figures (paper Figs. 4\u20135)\n",
    "\n",
    "Regenerates the two result figures from the paper directly from `all_results` above.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "order = [\"Camera-only\", \"Simple-concatenation\", \"Cross-attention (full)\",\n",
    "         \"Cross-attention (w/o LiDAR)\", \"Cross-attention (w/o radar)\"]\n",
    "labels = [\"Camera-\\nonly\", \"Simple-\\nconcat.\", \"Cross-attn.\\n(full)\",\n",
    "          \"Cross-attn.\\n(w/o LiDAR)\", \"Cross-attn.\\n(w/o radar)\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "tpr = [all_results[k][\"tpr_mean\"] * 100 for k in order]\n",
    "tpr_e = [all_results[k][\"tpr_std\"] * 100 for k in order]\n",
    "fpr = [all_results[k][\"fpr_mean\"] * 100 for k in order]\n",
    "fpr_e = [all_results[k][\"fpr_std\"] * 100 for k in order]\n",
    "\n",
    "x = np.arange(len(order))\n",
    "w = 0.35\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(9, 5))\n",
    "b1 = ax.bar(x - w/2, tpr, w, yerr=tpr_e, capsize=4, label=\"TPR (%)\", color=\"#2e7d32\")\n",
    "b2 = ax.bar(x + w/2, fpr, w, yerr=fpr_e, capsize=4, label=\"FPR (%)\", color=\"#c62828\")\n",
    "ax.set_xticks(x); ax.set_xticklabels(labels, fontsize=9)\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(\"Rate (%)\"); ax.set_ylim(0, 110)\n",
    "ax.set_title(\"Fig. 4. Synthetic Feasibility Study: TPR/FPR by Configuration\\n\"\n",
    "             \"(mean \\u00b1 std, n=3 seeded runs; synthetic proxy data)\")\n",
    "ax.legend(); ax.grid(axis=\"y\", alpha=0.25)\n",
    "for b in list(b1) + list(b2):\n",
    "    h = b.get_height()\n",
    "    ax.annotate(f\"{h:.1f}\", (b.get_x() + b.get_width()/2, h), textcoords=\"offset points\",\n",
    "                xytext=(0, 3), ha=\"center\", fontsize=8)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig(\"fig4_main_comparison.png\", dpi=200, bbox_inches=\"tight\")\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "abl_order = [\"Cross-attention (full)\", \"Cross-attention (w/o LiDAR)\", \"Cross-attention (w/o radar)\"]\n",
    "abl_labels = [\"Full\\n(Cam+LiDAR+Radar)\", \"w/o LiDAR\\n(Cam+Radar)\", \"w/o Radar\\n(Cam+LiDAR)\"]\n",
    "metrics = [\"tpr_mean\", \"fpr_mean\", \"f1_mean\", \"auc_mean\"]\n",
    "metric_labels = [\"TPR\", \"FPR\", \"F1\", \"AUC\"]\n",
    "colors = [\"#2e7d32\", \"#c62828\", \"#1565c0\", \"#6a1b9a\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "x = np.arange(len(abl_order))\n",
    "w = 0.2\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(9, 5))\n",
    "for i, (m, ml, c) in enumerate(zip(metrics, metric_labels, colors)):\n",
    "    vals = [all_results[k][m] * 100 for k in abl_order]\n",
    "    ax.bar(x + (i - 1.5) * w, vals, w, label=ml, color=c)\n",
    "ax.set_xticks(x); ax.set_xticklabels(abl_labels, fontsize=9)\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(\"Value (%) \\u2014 F1/AUC \\u00d7100 for scale\"); ax.set_ylim(0, 110)\n",
    "ax.set_title(\"Fig. 5. Modality-Ablation Comparison (mean, n=3 seeded runs;\\nsynthetic proxy data)\")\n",
    "ax.legend(ncol=4, loc=\"upper center\", bbox_to_anchor=(0.5, -0.15))\n",
    "ax.grid(axis=\"y\", alpha=0.25)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig(\"fig5_ablation_comparison.png\", dpi=200, bbox_inches=\"tight\")\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
